    "text": "The refactoring is substantial, so I'll deliver it in stages. Here's the plan:\n\n1. **`benchlib/process.py`** \u2014 a shared `EngineProcess` supervisor (spawn, watchdog, graceful QUIT, guaranteed kill on cancellation/failure) plus a `GpuSampler` context manager.\n2. **`benchlib/config.py`** \u2014 strict config loading/validation (`benchlib.toml`-style JSON with required keys, path checks, env allowlist).\n3. **`benchlib/artifacts.py`** \u2014 reusable manifest/rounds/requests/log writers with atomic writes.\n4. **`benchlib/protocol.py`** \u2014 wire protocol parsing (READY/ERR/T/DONE/STOP) shared by both harnesses.\n5. **`benchlib/analysis.py`** \u2014 deterministic row analysis (acceptance, TPS, oracle math) as pure functions.\n6. **`tools/bench_dflash_matrix.py`** \u2014 thin CLI over the library.\n7. **`tools/check_verify_scratch.py`** \u2014 thin CLI reusing supervisor/config/artifacts.\n8. **`tools/analyze_window_union.py`** + tests \u2014 refactored into pure functions with the same oracle semantics, plus a `bench",
