    "text": "The refactoring has substantial content. I'll deliver it in parts: this response covers the design overview, the shared process supervisor, and the benchmark command. The next response will cover the analysis tool, the parity checker, and the tests.\n\n## Design overview\n\n**Package layout** (all modules live under `tools/` as before, but as a coherent package `benchkit`):\n\n```\ntools/\n  benchkit/\n    __init__.py\n    config.py          # strict config loading + validation\n    process.py         # ProcessSupervisor: spawn, watchdog, cancellation, guaranteed teardown\n    artifacts.py       # ArtifactWriter: manifest/log/records writing, hashing\n    analysis.py        # window-union analysis (pure functions, moved from analyze_window_union)\n    parity.py          # numeric comparison helpers for verify-scratch\n    runner.py          # benchmark command (bench_dflash_matrix)\n    verify_scratch.py  # check_verify_scratch command\n    __main__.py        # `python -m benchkit <command>` CLI\n  test_benchkit_analysis.py\n  test_benchkit_process.py\n  test_benchkit_runner.py\n```\n\n**Key decisions:**\n\n1. **`ProcessSupervisor`** \u2014 one class",
